mechanism:
NO-GO (theory), in four steps. (1) Factoring lemma (new; generalises R1-R4, R9 and Barkoutsos eq. 12). Suppose the consumer sees the quantum distribution p only through one of: (a) argmin E; (b) E-order statistics; (c) the minimiser of a convex functional over distributions of the form g(E); (d) E_p[f] for a fixed classical f. Then the output equals Phi(Prim(E)), where Prim is minimum finding, sampling from g(E), or mean estimation. Any classical algorithm for Prim at the same query count therefore reproduces the pipeline. (2) Known tight black-box bounds for each primitive:
- minimum finding: Theta(sqrt(N/k)) (BBBV, Durr-Hoyer);
- prior-to-posterior resampling: Theta(P_acc^-1/2) (Ozols-Roetteler-Roland);
- walk-access sampling: quadratic gap amplification is optimal for frustration-free (Markov-chain) Hamiltonians in Somma-Boixo's black-box model, which gives Omega(delta^-1/2);
- estimation: Omega(sigma/eps) (Nayak-Wu, Heinrich, Chen-Nannicini).
(3) Composition lemma (I(prog)): if each primitive in a sequential or nested composition is at most quadratic in its own classical cost, the whole composition is at most quadratic in total classical cost. (4) The exception, and why this is NOT 'everything is quadratic'. In the pure value-query model for optimisation, poly(n) quantum vs exp(n^(1/5-o(1))) classical queries is proven: GHV (STOC 2021) led to LWWZ 2025, for discrete objectives and for box-constrained continuous objectives via QHD. For total Boolean functions, Aaronson et al. give only D=O(Q^4). So the ceiling is a theorem only in the chain-access and needle parameterisations above. The screening rule that follows: any protein claim beyond quadratic must show GHV-type oracle structure (card 8) or planted algebraic structure (card 12) in the energy. Everything else a classical computer copies, because the consumer only ever sees Prim(E).

oracle_and_state_prep:
Both sides are charged the same:
- O_E is coherent; the literature-phase I(agent) estimate is ~1e6-1e8 Toffolis per call at L=100, i.e. a per-call cost ratio R of about 1e7-1e10 vs classical;
- W(P) is built from O_E plus a Metropolis coin;
- U_0 is exact product-state loading of the per-residue (theta,tau) head, O(L) rotations.
The theorem does not depend on oracle cost; that cost only makes the ceiling worse in wall-clock.

