kill_result:
Either kills the lead:
- MSM estimates give delta/Phi^2 <= 10 (diffusive) at every L in 44-120 aa, so lifts can match the walk;
- delta is not small at all (t_2 <= 1e6 steps).

Either kills it:
- all deep modes found by long PT at 44-150 aa are recovered by DG from a polynomial number of bin-choice combinations (case A everywhere), so the separation is dequantised;
- no narrow deep mode carries >=1% of posterior mass at the posterior temperature (no hide-and-seek structure at all).

Any one of these kills it:
- C_v peak height per residue does not grow with L, and energy histograms at the peak are unimodal at 45-120 aa (no first-order character);
- learned-Q umbrella or 2-D Wang-Landau gives round-trip times polynomial in L with degree <=3;
- the Lee-Kosterlitz DeltaF extrapolates below 2 ln R (about 32-46 kT) for L <= 300.

Either kills it:
- a protein-relevant energy whose gradients are unavailable or cost >> c*S (for example a black-box score with discrete repacking, or external docking), making value-only access the true classical model;
- a separation proven against derivative-query classical algorithms (that would belong to card 4 or 8, not this one).

Either kills the lead:
- a proof that pair-additive (bounded-description) energies with explicit coordinates admit classical algorithms that match QHD or adiabatic paths whenever those are polynomial;
- a demonstration that the LWWZ continuous construction needs features that 28-bin pair splines lack: body order growing with n, Lipschitz constants exponential in n, or a domain chain geometry cannot reach.

